#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119574 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b02f02f1-f270-55e0-a7a9-0b729c4d82c0" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Parametric Equation of the Plane Parallel To Two Given Vectors"}] :question/id #uuid "a6fded96-287a-53ee-8b1c-dd618562b2c2" :question/math-academy-id "e-4940" :question/problem "Find a parametric equation of the plane that passes through the point $P(-3,2,5)$ and is parallel to the vectors $\\mathbf{b}= \\langle 17,3,15 \\rangle$  and $\\mathbf{c}= \\langle 5,0,-8 \\rangle.$" :question/worked-solution "A parametric equation of a plane is given by \n\n$$\n\\mathbf{r}=\\mathbf{p}+ s\\mathbf{b}+ t \\mathbf{c},\n$$\n\nwhere $\\mathbf{p}$ is the position vector of a point on the plane and the vectors $\\mathbf{b}$ and $\\mathbf{c}$ are parallel to the plane but not to each other.\n\nHere, the position vector of the given point $P$ is $\\mathbf{p}=\\langle -3,2,5 \\rangle,$ and the two vectors that are parallel to the plane (but not to each other) are $\\mathbf{b}= \\langle 17,3,15 \\rangle$ and $\\mathbf{c}= \\langle 5,0,-8 \\rangle.$\n\nSo, a parametric equation of the plane is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =⟨-3,2,5⟩+s\\,⟨17,3,15⟩+t\\,⟨5,0,-8⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119575 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3061cb06-f57f-57c8-8821-dbd962b1e78e" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Parametric Equation of the Plane Parallel To Two Lines"}] :question/id #uuid "297bda8f-6e33-5cc2-a2e1-5ab6186fa9d0" :question/math-academy-id "e-4941" :question/problem "Find a parametric equation of the plane that passes through the point $C(2,50,-19)$ and is parallel to the lines $\\mathbf{r}= \\langle 2,\\sqrt{6},17 \\rangle + s \\langle -1,7,2 \\rangle$ and $\\mathbf{r}= \\langle 20,-44, 27 \\rangle + t \\langle 2\\sqrt{3},9,-8 \\rangle$." :question/worked-solution "The direction vectors of the lines are $\\mathbf{v_1}=\\langle  -1,7,2  \\rangle$ and $\\mathbf{v_2}=\\langle 2\\sqrt{3},9,-8 \\rangle$, respectively. These vectors are parallel to the plane but not to each other.\n\nWe also know that the point $C(2,50,-19)$ lies on the plane and its position vector is $\\mathbf{c}=\\langle 2,50,-19 \\rangle.$  \n\nSo, the corresponding parametric equation of the plane is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =c+s{v}_{1}+t{v}_{2} \\\\ r & =⟨2,50,-19⟩+s\\,⟨-1,7,2⟩+t\\,⟨2\\sqrt{3},9,-8⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119576 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d11f13f0-1cfa-59ec-a04a-9483d942b1aa" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Parametric Equation of the Plane Passing Through Three Given Points"}] :question/id #uuid "9c36ddd5-fcf1-5c4d-a350-aa8ef3a3ca9e" :question/math-academy-id "e-4942" :question/problem "Find a parametric equation of the plane that passes through the points $A(-1,4,-3),$ $B(7,5,4),$ and $C(2,-2,8).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find two vectors that are parallel to the plane (but not to each other). Let's use the displacement vectors $\\overrightarrow{AB}$ and $\\overrightarrow{AC},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =⟨7,5,4⟩-⟨-1,4,-3⟩ \\\\  & =⟨8,1,7⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =⟨2,-2,8⟩-⟨-1,4,-3⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3,-6,11⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, if we consider the position vector $\\mathbf{a}=\\langle -1,4,-3 \\rangle$ of the point $A,$ then the corresponding parametric equation of the plane is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =a+s\\overset{\\to }{AB}+t\\overset{\\to }{AC} \\\\ r & =⟨-1,4,-3⟩+s⟨8,1,7⟩+t⟨3,-6,11⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Watch out!** The form of the final equation depends on our choice of vectors and the point on the plane. We could have picked other vectors. Likewise, we could have chosen $B$ or $C$ instead of $A$ as our point on the plane. So, the answer is *not unique*!"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119588 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "62196ae9-df2e-5a3a-bc0a-1c0f4c40af3e" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Normal Vector To a Plane Given by Parametric Equation"}] :question/id #uuid "b86eace4-01cb-5601-8e9b-2658e81fc656" :question/math-academy-id "e-5884" :question/problem "Find a normal vector to the plane \n\n$$\n\\mathbf{r}= \\langle -6,3, 2 \\rangle + t \\langle 4, 2, -1 \\rangle + s \\langle 4, -3, 2 \\rangle,\\qquad t,\\,s \\in (-\\infty,\\infty).\n$$" :question/worked-solution "From the parametric equation, we have that $\\mathbf{v} = \\langle 4, 2, -1 \\rangle$ and $\\mathbf{w} = \\langle 4, -3, 2 \\rangle$ are parallel to the plane.\n\nNow, we need to find a normal vector of the plane. To do that, we use the cross product of $\\mathbf{v}$ and $\\mathbf{w}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & =v\\times w \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]\\times [\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 4 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 4 & -3 & 2\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =i-12j-20k \\\\  & =⟨1,-12,-20⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, a normal vector to the plane is $\\mathbf{n}=\\langle 1, -12, -20 \\rangle.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186312062 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b02f02f1-f270-55e0-a7a9-0b729c4d82c0" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Parametric Equation of the Plane Parallel To Two Given Vectors"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ffa95c77-2ba8-5cf8-8e5b-104b48cb3d67" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨2,5,3⟩+s⟨-2,4,1⟩+t⟨3,1,-1⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312064} {:answer/id #uuid "edbc1d96-2326-592b-bfe6-8d8696cda3c8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨2,-5,3⟩+s⟨2,4,1⟩+t⟨3,-1,1⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312065} {:answer/id #uuid "97f33521-06aa-5680-8ce9-67c72fff3e18" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨2,-3,5⟩+s⟨2,4,1⟩+t⟨1,3,-1⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312066} {:answer/id #uuid "ed8bdeaf-4c6f-5932-87e5-444d1035d637" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨2,3,5⟩+s⟨1,-4,2⟩+t⟨1,3,1⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312067} {:answer/id #uuid "e96c5fa7-7c0b-5442-9053-ca24a4bc95eb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨2,-5,3⟩+s⟨4,2,1⟩+t⟨1,3,-1⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312068}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "97f33521-06aa-5680-8ce9-67c72fff3e18" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨2,-3,5⟩+s⟨2,4,1⟩+t⟨1,3,-1⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312066} :answer-field/id #uuid "24d50ff0-4013-516a-ac2d-c409781b79c1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312063}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "13d8a7ca-c38f-5c11-aa1b-651fc3654f5d" :question/math-academy-id "q-128463" :question/problem "Find a parametric equation of the plane that passes through the point $P(2,-3,5)$ and is parallel to the vectors ${v}_{1}=⟨2,4,1⟩$  and ${v}_{2}=⟨1,3,-1⟩.$" :question/worked-solution "A parametric equation of a plane is given by \n\n$$\nr=p+sb+tc,\n$$\n\nwhere $p$ is the position vector of a point on the plane and the vectors $b$ and $c$ are parallel to the plane but not to each other.\n\nHere, the position vector of the given point $P$ is $p=⟨2,-3,5⟩$ and the two vectors that are parallel to the plane (but not to each other) are ${v}_{1}=⟨2,4,1⟩$  and ${v}_{2}=⟨1,3,-1⟩.$\n\nSo, a parametric equation of the plane is given by\n\n$$\nr=⟨2,-3,5⟩+s⟨2,4,1⟩+t⟨1,3,-1⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186312069 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b02f02f1-f270-55e0-a7a9-0b729c4d82c0" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Parametric Equation of the Plane Parallel To Two Given Vectors"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "944e707d-89e4-580f-aba7-7d8ee794464e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]+s[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312071} {:answer/id #uuid "1830beae-83d0-505d-832d-f8be1c218587" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]+s[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312072} {:answer/id #uuid "c7c09f52-377f-56d4-b795-b3452fac5be4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]+s[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312073} {:answer/id #uuid "25bc43e3-849b-5f52-b947-b8f74e046cd3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]+s[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312074} {:answer/id #uuid "6e6f9a04-8dfd-5705-8af9-b2ffe6fe1e6e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]+s[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312075}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c7c09f52-377f-56d4-b795-b3452fac5be4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]+s[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312073} :answer-field/id #uuid "69ca3e02-6674-5400-87a6-6cf8fa389de8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312070}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b9e20786-5f2c-55c6-bc0f-010879e57039" :question/math-academy-id "q-128467" :question/problem "Find a parametric equation of the plane that passes through the point $S(1,-3,4)$ and is parallel to the vectors ${v}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]$  and ${v}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "A parametric equation of a plane is given by \n\n$$\nr=p+sb+tc,\n$$\n\nwhere $p$ is the position vector of a point on the plane and the vectors $b$ and $c$ are parallel to the plane but not to each other.\n\nHere, the position vector of the given point $S$ is $p=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]$, and the two vectors that are parallel to the plane (but not to each other) are ${v}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]$  and ${v}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$\n\nSo, a parametric equation of the plane is given by\n\n$$\nr=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]+s[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186312076 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3061cb06-f57f-57c8-8821-dbd962b1e78e" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Parametric Equation of the Plane Parallel To Two Lines"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "91ac9edb-fec4-5707-be50-fcbb480cf666" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨3,-2,7⟩+s⟨3,-1,5⟩+t⟨3,6,7⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312078} {:answer/id #uuid "aabeb61e-b320-529d-8444-6279bb150f50" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨7,2,3⟩+s⟨2,-1,2⟩+t⟨4,3,7⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312079} {:answer/id #uuid "1974de00-d585-539d-bb79-d49fae942a75" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨2,-7,3⟩+s⟨2,-4,1⟩+t⟨3,5,2⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312080} {:answer/id #uuid "d7a4e0cf-df0a-5da4-8318-83716ae162ca" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨7,-2,3⟩+s⟨2,-2,1⟩+t⟨3,4,7⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312081} {:answer/id #uuid "9639e8c5-a54f-5c6a-8405-3aa2b7d9068c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨7,-3,2⟩+s⟨3,-2,1⟩+t⟨7,4,3⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312082}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d7a4e0cf-df0a-5da4-8318-83716ae162ca" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨7,-2,3⟩+s⟨2,-2,1⟩+t⟨3,4,7⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312081} :answer-field/id #uuid "e64c26b3-76ef-5a06-88aa-856bcfb352cc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312077}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "6d8e167e-ba7b-5746-8896-10f0f88087c7" :question/math-academy-id "q-128501" :question/problem "Find a parametric equation of the plane that passes through the point $A(7,-2,3)$ and is parallel to the lines $r=⟨9,2,1⟩+s⟨2,-2,1⟩$ and $r=⟨4,-5,19⟩+t⟨3,4,7⟩.$" :question/worked-solution "The direction vectors of the lines are ${v}_{1}=⟨2,-2,1⟩$ and ${v}_{2}=⟨3,4,7⟩$, respectively. These vectors are parallel to the plane but not to each other.\n\nWe also know that the point $A(7,-2,3)$ lies on the plane and its position vector is $a=⟨7,-2,3⟩.$  \n\nSo, the corresponding parametric equation of the plane is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =a+s{v}_{1}+t{v}_{2} \\\\ r & =⟨7,-2,3⟩+s⟨2,-2,1⟩+t⟨3,4,7⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186312083 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3061cb06-f57f-57c8-8821-dbd962b1e78e" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Parametric Equation of the Plane Parallel To Two Lines"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a020b529-7917-522b-8a10-d35ed66552f6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨-7,-3,12⟩+s⟨3,3,1⟩+t⟨1,5,7⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312085} {:answer/id #uuid "01037a29-87fb-5534-9d29-9c6856056cd8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨-7,12,-3⟩+s⟨-3,5,1⟩+t⟨1,6,5⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312086} {:answer/id #uuid "368581f2-ac9d-5036-8fc0-83a1fa43877a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨-3,12,-7⟩+s⟨1,3,-5⟩+t⟨1,6,5⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312087} {:answer/id #uuid "3ee38ee8-91c2-5899-9d70-633e4ba87571" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨-7,12,-3⟩+s⟨-5,3,1⟩+t⟨1,5,6⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312088} {:answer/id #uuid "27a50bf8-a41e-5c85-8ffc-2169a0be0b25" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨-7,-3,12⟩+s⟨-3,4,2⟩+t⟨1,5,5⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312089}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3ee38ee8-91c2-5899-9d70-633e4ba87571" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨-7,12,-3⟩+s⟨-5,3,1⟩+t⟨1,5,6⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312088} :answer-field/id #uuid "6b10fbed-39b9-5e9d-8758-096fcf2624ae" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312084}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "4aa7cfeb-fc6c-587e-9b16-53483d3180f8" :question/math-academy-id "q-128536" :question/problem "Find a parametric equation of the plane that passes through the point $B(-7,12,-3)$ and is parallel to the lines $r=⟨-7,2,4⟩+s⟨-5,3,1⟩$ and $r=⟨-22,17,13⟩+t⟨1,5,6⟩.$" :question/worked-solution "The direction vectors of the lines are ${v}_{1}=⟨-5,3,1⟩$ and ${v}_{2}=⟨1,5,6⟩$, respectively. These vectors are parallel to the plane but not to each other.\n\nWe also know that the point $B(-7,12,-3)$ lies on the plane and its position vector is $b=⟨-7,12,-3⟩.$  \n\nSo, the corresponding parametric equation of the plane is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =b+s{v}_{1}+t{v}_{2} \\\\ r & =⟨-7,12,-3⟩+s⟨-5,3,1⟩+t⟨1,5,6⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186312090 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d11f13f0-1cfa-59ec-a04a-9483d942b1aa" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Parametric Equation of the Plane Passing Through Three Given Points"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "831c178f-3859-5788-96ce-9dd071542a9e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨3,2,-1⟩+s⟨0,-1,-1⟩+t⟨2,-1,3⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312092} {:answer/id #uuid "6e1f89fb-fd91-5160-aa6e-58fbd5d3c600" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨3,2,-1⟩+s⟨1,0,-1⟩+t⟨2,1,3⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312093} {:answer/id #uuid "96b18f8f-0e74-5b73-a205-349646b72522" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨3,2,-1⟩+s⟨0,-1,0⟩+t⟨2,-3,1⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312094} {:answer/id #uuid "458963d4-275c-5fe7-bb4e-cff7ba0ebf39" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨3,2,-1⟩+s⟨1,0,-1⟩+t⟨-1,3,2⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312095} {:answer/id #uuid "854f7b98-c641-5836-b207-6028f32f1f